WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.980
What has the actress who played Angela on
The Office been doing in the years since Dundler

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.280
Mifflin shut its doors?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.300
As it turns out, she's been keeping pretty
busy, even if we don't see her every week

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:10.800
anymore.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.320
Here's what Angela Kinsey is up to now.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.100
In 2014, Kinsey jumped on board the Hulu sitcom
The Hotwives of Orlando, a merciless parody

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.080
of the Real Housewives franchise.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.020
She starred alongside a bunch of other funny
ladies including Andrea Savage, Kristen Schaal,

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:27.980
and Casey Wilson.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.520
In Season 1, Kinsey played Crystal Simmons,
an Orlando weather girl who considers herself

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.260
a devout Christian but has never read the
Bible because it's, quote, "written in Jewish."

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.920
In season 2, almost all the returning cast
members assumed new roles as the Hotwives

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.640
series headed to Las Vegas.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.780
Kinsey's new character was Stephanie, an uptight
snob who created a rather unique food line.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.800
"I developed a food line called 'Anorexi-Yeah!'

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.820
You know, I just wanted to take that word
back."

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.180
Starting in 2016, Kinsey starred in the Netflix
sitcom Haters Back Off as Bethany, mother

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.720
of the clueless and talentless Miranda Sings.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.340
The show was an experiment in transforming
a YouTube sensation into a scripted TV show.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.360
Miranda Sings was the creation of Colleen
Ballinger, whose millions of online followers

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.580
had already gotten to know the arrogant and
hopeless Sings long before she made the jump

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.320
to Netflix.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.540
Ultimately, the experiment didn't last.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:24.240
After two seasons, 16 episodes, and mixed
reviews, Haters Back Off was canceled.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.020
But while critics may not have fallen in love
with the show as a whole, many singled out

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.470
Kinsey's performance as a reason to tune in.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.850
Robert Lloyd of the Los Angeles Times said,

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.860
"[Kinsey] takes the series from a twisted
lark to something deeper and grander."

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.040
"This is my casual brace, okay?

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.440
I need my seductive one."

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:48.100
In August 2016, Kinsey announced on Instagram
her engagement to her boyfriend Joshua Snyder.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.940
The proposal was quite adorable.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.340
Kinsey's then 8-year-old daughter Isabel told
her she wanted to show Kinsey the fort she

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.540
and Snyder's sons had made outside.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.360
But instead of a fort, a blanket was waiting
by their pool.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.740
The boys brought her flowers and Snyder brought
her an engagement ring.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.740
It was an emerald, the birthstone of all three
of their kids.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.360
The happy couple got married that November
in Topanga, California.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.480
Guests were given custom copper mugs, and
the wedding cake included a Lego cake topper

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.960
created by their children.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.480
Fans of The Office will either be disappointed
or relieved to learn that there were no reports

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.980
of butter cow sculptures.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.000
"I would like a cow butter sculpture of a
cat."

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:24.780
"That doesn't make any sense."

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.400
Angela Martin's love of cats was inspired
by Angela Kinsey's own love for the animals.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.709
She regularly posts pictures of her own kitties
to her Instagram account, and her generosity

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:39.310
goes beyond showing how cute her cats are,
as she's a dedicated supporter of organizations

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.620
devoted to helping cats.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:46.340
In 2014, Kinsey told the blog I Have Cat that
her work with charitable cat organizations

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.020
started with what she was doing with her own
free time.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.150
An old neighborhood of hers was crawling with
stray cats, and she would get them spayed

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.700
and neutered before releasing them back into
the neighborhood.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.640
She also discussed how she brought her love
for cats into her performance on The Office.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.960
While shooting the pilot episode, she improvised
a line where she invited everyone to a cat

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.720
birthday party and went so far as to pass
out post-it note invites to her castmates.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:14.749
In December 2016, Kinsey and her husband Josh
Snyder launched the webseries Baking With

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:16.380
Josh &amp; Ange on YouTube.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.239
The show was apparently Colleen Ballinger's
idea, who suggested it when Snyder brought

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.360
some cookies while visiting Kinsey on the
Haters Back Off set.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.680
Though initially intimidated by the idea of
having to deal with the necessary technology

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.240
required for a webseries, Kinsey and Snyder
gave it a go and they seem to be doing pretty

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:32.740
well.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.240
They've even had a guest appearance from Kinsey's
former TV husband, as Rainn Wilson stopped

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.680
by to make vegan brownies.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.760
He'd only recently started eating vegan, and
judging by his facial expressions, the brownie

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.400
experiment may not have been a phenomenal
success.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.920
"This is really good.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.340
You would never know it's vegan."

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.820
Apparently, you can buy clothes from vending
machines now.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.840
You may not have known that, but Angela Kinsey
does.

00:03:55.849 --> 00:04:01.109
In March 2018, she posted a video and multiple
shots of herself on her Instagram account,

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:04.020
announcing that she had bought a jacket from
an airport vending machine.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.180
Kinsey's followers and fans were so tickled
by this development that someone actually

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.980
created an Instagram account just for the
jacket.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:15.280
It has close to 30,000 followers, including,
of course, Kinsey herself.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.720
So if you're ever feeling like you need a
little humiliation, just remember, unless

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:24.270
you're super-popular on Instagram, there are
at least 30,000 people in the world who like

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.300
a jacket more than they like you.

